[281.048747, "o", "[user] fetch http://api.mock-sites.svc/data\r\n[model] call curl({\"arguments\":\"-s http://api.mock-sites.svc/data\"})\r\n[tool curl] error: {\"not-found\":\"no tool named curl in this workload\"}\r\n[model] Done. Here is what each step returned: curl: ERROR: {\"not-found\":\"no tool named curl in this workload\"}\r\n"]
[283.060221, "o", "\u001b[0;33m# The model asked for curl anyway, and the toolbox plugin refused: this workload has no curl. The \r\n# agent can only use what its manifest gives it: the harness itself imports no HTTP client, no files \r\n# and no sockets, so it has no way to fetch the page on its own. The model's last line starts with \r\n# \"Done.\" whatever the tools returned; it is a script, and it reports each result as it came back.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
