[500.57878, "o", "[user] fetch http://api.mock-sites.svc/data\r\n[model] call curl({\"arguments\":\"-s http://api.mock-sites.svc/data\"})\r\n[tool curl] ok: {\"service\":\"releases\",\"version\":\"1.2\",\"notes\":\"several bug fixes and performance improvements\"}\r\n[model] Done. Here is what each step returned: curl: {\"service\":\"releases\",\"version\":\"1.2\",\"notes\":\"several bug fixes and performance improvements\"}\r\n"]
[502.611615, "o", "\u001b[0;33m# The prompt that got \"no tool named curl\" in step 1. The host is in curl's `allowedHosts`, so the \r\n# mock API answers.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
