[514.8578, "o", "[user] save http://api.mock-sites.svc/data to page.html\r\n[model] call curl({\"arguments\":\"-o page.html -s http://api.mock-sites.svc/data\"})\r\n[tool curl] ok: saved 95 bytes to /data/page.html\r\n[model] Done. Here is what each step returned: curl: saved 95 bytes to /data/page.html\r\n"]
[516.952976, "o", "\u001b[0;33m# The model turns this into `curl -o page.html`. The prebuilt curl answers `saved 95 bytes to \r\n# /data/page.html`. Your build answers with the message you wrote, which shows your code is the one \r\n# running. The grant includes `/data`, so the write succeeds: the folder is the boundary, not a \r\n# blanket ban.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
