[654.805458, "o", "\u001b[0;33m# The same agent as step 2, with sqlite added (and listed with curl under `hostInterfaces`). Its \r\n# grant: one folder, read only, holding two databases (`main.db`, the talks, and `rooms.db`).\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[662.824723, "o", "\u001b[0;33m# The host pod also has a third database, `/workshop/private-data/payroll.db`, on its own disk. \r\n# Native sqlite3 on that machine would open it. No workload is granted that folder, and the host's \r\n# `hostPaths` list doesn't allow it, so no workload may even ask for it. See it on the host pod:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
