[942.546443, "o", "[user] triage the open PRs in wasmCloud/wasmCloud\r\n[model] call gh({\"arguments\":\"pr list -R wasmCloud/wasmCloud --limit 10\"})\r\n[tool gh] ok: 10 open pull requests in wasmCloud/wasmCloud, by updated (desc), page 1: #5898 feat: GPU benches for wasi:webgpu against native (by ricochet, main <- wasmCloud:feat/gpubench, updated 2026-11-08) [draft] #5913 fix(wash-runtime): bound wasi:webgpu waits and survive device loss (by ricochet, main <- wa...\r\n[model] Done. Here is what each step returned: gh: 10 open pull requests in wasmCloud/wasmCloud, by updated (desc), page 1: #5898 feat: GPU benches for wasi:webgpu against\r\n"]
[944.563605, "o", "\u001b[0;33m# The model turns this into `gh pr list -R wasmCloud/wasmCloud --limit 10`:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[948.585761, "o", "\u001b[0;33m# Each line is one pull request: number, title, author, branches, last update, and labels and \r\n# requested reviewers when there are any.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[954.605405, "o", "\u001b[0;33m# 3. One pull request (allowed) \u001b[0m\r\n"]
[956.623454, "o", "\u001b[0;33m# Pick any number from your list. The commands here use #5885, which is merged, so it reads the same \r\n# for everyone.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
