[1014.383312, "o", "[user] curl -s https://api.github.com/repos/wasmCloud/wasmCloud/pulls\r\n[model] call curl({\"arguments\":\"-s https://api.github.com/repos/wasmCloud/wasmCloud/pulls\"})\r\n[tool curl] error: {\"access-denied\":\"api.github.com: this tool may not reach that host (not in its allowedHosts)\"}\r\n[model] Done. Here is what each step returned: curl: ERROR: {\"access-denied\":\"api.github.com: this tool may not reach that host (not in its allowedHosts)\"}\r\n"]
[1016.397314, "o", "\u001b[0;33m# `access-denied: api.github.com: this tool may not reach that host`. Signed in or not, curl's \r\n# `allowedHosts` is the mock API host alone, and curl holds no token anyway. Nor is there a token \r\n# file for it to read: the plugin keeps the token in its memory and writes it nowhere, and curl's \r\n# only folder is `/data`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
